# ReRoute frontend environment template
#
# Copy this file to `frontend/.env.local` for local overrides (Vite reads
# `.env`, `.env.local`, `.env.development`, `.env.production`, and the matching
# `.env.<mode>.local` files). `.env.local` is the usual choice because it is
# meant for personal, machine-specific values.
#
#   Copy-Item "frontend/.env.example" "frontend/.env.local"
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WARNING: NEVER COMMIT REAL SECRETS HERE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything a `VITE_`-prefixed variable holds is inlined into the built
# JavaScript bundle and is readable by anyone who loads the page. SAP secrets
# belong in the backend `backend/.env` only; there is no frontend variable that
# needs one.
#
# IMPORTANT: as of this commit `frontend/.gitignore` does not ignore `.env*`
# files, so a real `.env.local` is not protected by git. Add that ignore rule
# yourself before you create one, and check `git status` before every commit.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed with `VITE_` to client code, through
# `import.meta.env`. Anything without that prefix stays on the build machine.
# A variable also has to exist at `vite build` time: a value set only in the
# Vercel/Render dashboard after the build has already run will not be baked in,
# so re-deploy after changing it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


# Absolute origin of the ReRoute backend, with no trailing slash and no path.
#
# Leave this blank for local development. The frontend then calls the same
# origin it is served from, and `frontend/vite.config.js` proxies `/audit` and
# `/session` to http://127.0.0.1:8000. Note the deliberate asymmetry: the dev
# proxy covers only those two prefixes, so `/health`, `/skills/*`, `/route`,
# `/match`, `/market/*`, and `/employer/*` are NOT proxied. A blank value
# therefore only works for the endpoints that are proxied; for the rest, fill in
# the variable line at the end of this file.
#
# Set it for split hosting (Vercel frontend + Render/Railway backend), where
# there is no dev proxy and nothing is same-origin. The value must then also be
# allowed by the backend's CORS_ORIGINS, and it must be https once the frontend
# itself is https or the browser will block the request.
#
# WebSocket note: the agent stream URL is derived from this value by
# `frontend/src/lib/sessionSocket.js`, which converts the scheme http->ws and
# https->wss and appends `/session/<id>/stream`. There is no separate WS
# variable, so this single origin decides both REST and WebSocket traffic. With
# the value blank, the socket falls back to the page origin, which is only
# correct when the backend shares that origin.
#
# The demo-mode toggle ignores this variable: when demoMode is on, the frontend
# deliberately forces http://127.0.0.1:8000 (see DEFAULT_BACKEND_BASE_URL in
# frontend/src/api.js) so a presenter can bypass a flaky hosted backend.
#
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Demo-mode storage key — NOT configurable
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# `DEMO_MODE_STORAGE_KEY` in `frontend/src/context/DemoModeContext.jsx` is the
# literal string `reroute:demo-mode`. It is a hardcoded constant, not an env
# var, so there is deliberately no VITE_ variable for it and none is documented
# here. The toggle is read from and written to `localStorage` under that key and
# defaults to ON.
